 "rule": "for k in {2,4,8} and draw in {0,1,2}: order candidate sources by ascending sha256('pooled-encoder-0.2|D|k' + k + '|draw' + draw + '|' + dataset); the arm uses the first k sources in that order that are eligible (at least W_max/8 inner-training windows, counted at P2)",
 "rule_status": "quoted unchanged from ALLOCATION.json d_arms.rule; its last part (an arm uses the first k eligible sources) is replaced from protocol revision 3 by arm_rule below",
 "candidate_note": "conditional sources (area2, falcon_m1) join the candidate list only if admitted before the freeze; the orders are then recomputed with the same rule and recorded in MIXTURE-MANIFEST.json",
 "arm_rule": "A source is eligible for the D arms if it has at least W_max/8 unique inner-training windows. A source enters a k-source arm (k in {2, 4, 8}) only if it has at least W_max/k unique inner-training windows. For each k and each draw, the order of that draw in D-ARM-ORDERS.json is walked from the top: a source that is not eligible, or that has fewer than W_max/k windows (short for this k), is skipped, and the first k sources that remain form the arm. Each source of the arm gives W_max/k unique windows: the first W_max/k of its inner-training windows in the fixed hash order (the window order of ALLOCATION.json q_window_rule, applied to that source). A skipped source stays available to the arms with a larger k and to D_all. D_all takes floor(W_max / n) unique windows from each of the n eligible sources, in the same window order.",
 "arm_rule_note": "ALLOCATION.json is not edited. The last part of its rule (an arm uses the first k eligible sources of its order) is replaced from protocol revision 3 by the arm rule above; the ordering part of the rule and the nine orders are unchanged.",
 "key": "sha256 of the UTF-8 text 'pooled-encoder-0.2|D|k<k>|draw<draw>|<dataset>', ascending by its hex digest (equal digests, which do not occur, would be ordered by name)",
